WEBVTT
X-TIMESTAMP-MAP=LOCAL:00:00:00.000,MPEGTS:0

00:01.632 --> 00:05.536 align:center line:79%
33 years ago, I received my call
to serve as a missionary

00:05.636 --> 00:07.237 align:center line:81%
in the Utah Ogden Mission.

00:07.804 --> 00:11.475 align:center line:79%
Of course, coming from Europe,
some local Utah traditions,

00:11.475 --> 00:14.011 align:center line:81%
like “green Jell-O with carrots” and

00:14.011 --> 00:17.114 align:center line:79%
“funeral potatoes” were
a bit peculiar to me!

00:18.715 --> 00:20.984 align:center line:79%
However, I was deeply
impressed by the devotion

00:20.984 --> 00:23.287 align:center line:81%
and discipleship of many of the Saints,

00:23.520 --> 00:26.356 align:center line:79%
the sheer number of people
attending Church meetings,

00:26.356 --> 00:29.359 align:center line:79%
and the scale of fully
functioning Church programs.

00:29.960 --> 00:31.628 align:center line:81%
When my mission came to an end,

00:31.695 --> 00:35.632 align:center line:79%
I wanted to make sure that the joy
I felt and the spiritual strength

00:35.632 --> 00:39.970 align:center line:79%
and maturity I observed would also
be available for my future family.

00:40.404 --> 00:42.205 align:center line:81%
I was determined to return quickly

00:42.205 --> 00:45.442 align:center line:79%
to live my life in the “shadows
of the everlasting hills.”

00:46.343 --> 00:48.312 align:center line:81%
However, the Lord had different plans.

00:48.712 --> 00:50.247 align:center line:81%
On my first Sunday at home,

00:50.247 --> 00:54.451 align:center line:79%
my wise bishop called me to serve
as the Young Men president in our ward.

00:54.451 --> 00:56.386 align:center line:81%
Serving this wonderful group of young men,

00:56.386 --> 00:59.790 align:center line:79%
I quickly learned that the joy
that comes from being a disciple

00:59.790 --> 01:03.727 align:center line:79%
of Christ has very little
to do with the size of Church meetings

01:03.827 --> 01:05.562 align:center line:81%
or the scale of programs.

01:06.430 --> 01:10.334 align:center line:79%
So when I married my beautiful wife,
Margret, we joyfully decided to stay

01:10.334 --> 01:13.737 align:center line:79%
in Europe and raise our family
in our home country of Germany.

01:14.304 --> 01:16.773 align:center line:79%
Together, we witnessed what
President Russell M. Nelson taught

01:16.773 --> 01:21.345 align:center line:79%
many years ago: “The joy we feel has
little to do with the circumstances

01:21.345 --> 01:25.582 align:center line:79%
of our lives, and everything
to do with the focus of our lives.”

01:26.183 --> 01:29.786 align:center line:79%
When the focus of our life is on Christ
and His gospel message,

01:30.153 --> 01:34.291 align:center line:79%
we can experience the full blessings
of discipleship wherever we live.

01:35.425 --> 01:39.630 align:center line:79%
However, in a world that's increasingly
secular, complex, and confusing,

01:39.763 --> 01:42.933 align:center line:79%
with different and often
conflicting messages and demands,

01:43.266 --> 01:47.971 align:center line:79%
how can we avoid our eyes becoming
blinded and our hearts becoming hardened,

01:48.105 --> 01:49.773 align:center line:81%
and remain focused on the “plain

01:49.773 --> 01:52.743 align:center line:79%
and precious things”
of the gospel of Jesus Christ?

01:53.810 --> 01:55.245 align:center line:81%
During a time of confusion,

01:55.245 --> 02:00.384 align:center line:79%
the Apostle Paul gave great advice
to the Saints of Corinth by reminding them

02:00.384 --> 02:03.687 align:center line:79%
to focus on “the simplicity
that is in Christ.”

02:04.755 --> 02:05.856 align:center line:81%
The doctrine of Christ

02:05.889 --> 02:08.959 align:center line:79%
and the law of the gospel are so
simple that even little

02:08.959 --> 02:10.594 align:center line:81%
children can understand them.

02:11.094 --> 02:13.730 align:center line:79%
We can access the redeeming
power of Jesus Christ

02:13.730 --> 02:16.933 align:center line:79%
and receive all spiritual
blessings our Heavenly Father has prepared

02:16.933 --> 02:22.072 align:center line:79%
for us by exercising faith in Jesus
Christ, repenting, being baptized,

02:22.239 --> 02:26.443 align:center line:79%
being sanctified through the gift of the
Holy Ghost, and enduring to the end.

02:27.010 --> 02:28.879 align:center line:79%
President Nelson has
described this journey

02:28.879 --> 02:30.947 align:center line:81%
so beautifully as the “covenant path”

02:30.947 --> 02:34.785 align:center line:79%
and the process of becoming a “devout
disciple of Jesus Christ.”

02:35.719 --> 02:39.623 align:center line:79%
If this message is so simple,
why does it often feel so challenging

02:39.690 --> 02:42.592 align:center line:79%
to live Christ’s law
and follow His example?

02:42.592 --> 02:45.962 align:center line:79%
It may be that we misinterpret
simplicity as something that is easy

02:45.962 --> 02:49.066 align:center line:79%
to achieve without
without effort or diligence.

02:49.599 --> 02:53.670 align:center line:79%
Following Christ's law requires
constant effort and continual change.

02:54.104 --> 02:58.008 align:center line:79%
We need to “[put] off the natural
man and ... [become like a little] child.”

02:58.008 --> 03:00.610 align:center line:79%
This includes putting
our “trust in the Lord”

03:00.610 --> 03:04.347 align:center line:79%
and letting the complexity go, just
as little children do.

03:05.482 --> 03:07.984 align:center line:79%
Applying the doctrine
of Christ in a simplified

03:07.984 --> 03:12.155 align:center line:79%
and focused way will help us
to find joy in our daily lives,

03:12.355 --> 03:14.291 align:center line:81%
give guidance in our callings,

03:14.524 --> 03:17.461 align:center line:79%
answer some of life’s
most complex questions,

03:17.561 --> 03:20.497 align:center line:79%
and provide strength to face
our greatest challenges.

03:21.531 --> 03:25.736 align:center line:79%
But how can we practically implement
this simplicity in our lifelong journey

03:25.769 --> 03:27.370 align:center line:81%
as disciples of Christ?

03:27.738 --> 03:32.576 align:center line:79%
President Nelson reminded us
to focus on “pure truth, pure doctrine,

03:32.576 --> 03:38.048 align:center line:79%
and pure revelation” as we seek
to follow the Savior. Regularly asking

03:38.281 --> 03:40.717 align:center line:79%
“What would the Lord Jesus
Christ have me do?”

03:40.984 --> 03:42.853 align:center line:81%
reveals profound direction.

03:43.687 --> 03:48.325 align:center line:79%
Following His example provides a safe
path through uncertainty and a loving,

03:48.325 --> 03:50.560 align:center line:81%
guiding hand to hold from day to day.

03:51.561 --> 03:54.698 align:center line:79%
He is the Prince of Peace
and the Good Shepherd.

03:55.098 --> 03:57.167 align:center line:81%
He is our Comforter and Deliverer.

03:57.601 --> 03:59.503 align:center line:81%
He is our Rock and Refuge.

04:00.036 --> 04:03.907 align:center line:81%
He is a Friend—your friend and my friend!

04:04.574 --> 04:08.945 align:center line:79%
He invites us all to love God, keep
his commandments, and love our neighbor.

04:10.380 --> 04:14.351 align:center line:79%
As we choose to follow His example
and move forward with faith in Christ,

04:14.351 --> 04:17.821 align:center line:79%
embrace the power of His Atonement,
and remember our covenants,

04:17.821 --> 04:19.256 align:center line:81%
love fills our heart,

04:19.456 --> 04:21.558 align:center line:81%
hope and healing raise our spirits,

04:21.825 --> 04:24.461 align:center line:79%
and bitterness and sorrow
are replaced by gratitude

04:24.461 --> 04:27.497 align:center line:79%
and the patience
to wait for promised blessings.

04:27.497 --> 04:31.034 align:center line:79%
At times, we may need to distance
ourselves from an unhealthy situation

04:31.034 --> 04:32.402 align:center line:81%
or seek professional help.

04:32.903 --> 04:36.072 align:center line:79%
But in every case, applying
simple gospel principles will help

04:36.072 --> 04:39.242 align:center line:79%
us navigate through life's
challenges in the Lord's way.

04:40.076 --> 04:43.380 align:center line:79%
We sometimes underestimate
the strength we receive from simple

04:43.380 --> 04:47.684 align:center line:79%
acts like prayer, fasting,
scripture study, daily repentance,

04:47.717 --> 04:51.521 align:center line:79%
partaking of the sacrament weekly,
and regular temple attendance.

04:51.521 --> 04:54.991 align:center line:79%
But when we recognize that we don’t
need to “do some great thing,”

04:54.991 --> 04:58.495 align:center line:79%
and we center ourselves on applying
pure and simple doctrine,

04:58.695 --> 05:02.132 align:center line:79%
we start to see how the gospel
“works wonderfully” for us,

05:02.132 --> 05:04.568 align:center line:79%
even in the most challenging
circumstances.

05:04.801 --> 05:07.237 align:center line:79%
We find strength
and “confidence before God,”

05:07.237 --> 05:09.139 align:center line:81%
even when we experience heartache.

05:09.606 --> 05:12.609 align:center line:79%
Elder M. Russell Ballard
has reminded us many times,

05:12.609 --> 05:17.214 align:center line:79%
“It is in that simplicity that [we]
will find ... peace, joy, and happiness.”

05:18.181 --> 05:19.649 align:center line:81%
Applying the simplicity that is

05:19.649 --> 05:23.253 align:center line:79%
in Christ makes us
prioritize people over processes,

05:23.653 --> 05:26.656 align:center line:79%
eternal relationships
over short-term behaviors.

05:27.224 --> 05:30.327 align:center line:79%
We focus on “the things that matter most”
in God’s work of salvation

05:30.327 --> 05:34.664 align:center line:79%
and exaltation instead of getting
caught up in managing our ministering.

05:35.198 --> 05:38.969 align:center line:79%
We we make ourselves free to prioritize
the things we can do

05:39.169 --> 05:42.372 align:center line:79%
rather than being weighed
down by the things we cannot do.

05:42.372 --> 05:43.807 align:center line:81%
The Lord reminded us:

05:43.840 --> 05:47.177 align:center line:79%
“Wherefore, be not weary in well-doing,
for ye are laying the foundation

05:47.177 --> 05:49.479 align:center line:81%
of a great work. And out of

05:49.512 --> 05:52.616 align:center line:79%
small things
proceedeth that which is great.

05:52.616 --> 05:56.353 align:center line:79%
What powerful encouragement
to act in simplicity and humility,

05:56.553 --> 05:58.622 align:center line:81%
whatever our circumstances are.

05:59.856 --> 06:02.025 align:center line:81%
My grandmother, Marta Cziesla

06:02.392 --> 06:06.363 align:center line:79%
(the woman on the right in this picture)
was a wonderful example of doing “small

06:06.363 --> 06:09.032 align:center line:79%
and simple things”
to bring great things to pass.

06:09.032 --> 06:11.134 align:center line:81%
We lovingly called her “Oma Cziesla.”

06:11.902 --> 06:14.671 align:center line:79%
Oma embraced the gospel
in the small village of Selbongen

06:14.671 --> 06:17.307 align:center line:79%
in East Prussia together
with my great-grandmother

06:17.307 --> 06:22.112 align:center line:79%
on May 30th, 1926. She loved
the Lord and His gospel

06:22.112 --> 06:25.548 align:center line:79%
and was determined to keep
the covenants she had made.

06:25.548 --> 06:29.619 align:center line:79%
In 1930, she married my grandfather,
who was not a member of the Church.

06:30.053 --> 06:33.590 align:center line:79%
At this point, it became impossible
for Oma to attend Church meetings

06:33.590 --> 06:36.326 align:center line:79%
because my grandfather's
farm was many hours away from

06:36.326 --> 06:37.694 align:center line:81%
the nearest congregation.

06:38.395 --> 06:40.297 align:center line:81%
But she focused on what she could do.

06:40.764 --> 06:44.868 align:center line:79%
Oma continued to pray, read the
scriptures, and sing the songs of Zion.

06:45.435 --> 06:48.972 align:center line:79%
Some people might have thought
she was no longer active in her faith,

06:48.972 --> 06:50.774 align:center line:81%
but that was far from the truth.

06:51.341 --> 06:54.044 align:center line:79%
When my aunt and my father were born,
with no priesthood

06:54.044 --> 06:57.714 align:center line:79%
in the home and no Church
meetings or access to ordinances nearby,

06:57.714 --> 07:02.252 align:center line:79%
she again did what she could do and
focused on teaching her children “to pray

07:02.385 --> 07:04.487 align:center line:81%
and to walk uprightly before the Lord.”

07:04.988 --> 07:09.025 align:center line:79%
She read to them from the scriptures,
sang with them the songs of Zion,

07:09.025 --> 07:11.428 align:center line:81%
and of course prayed with them—every day.

07:11.962 --> 07:15.198 align:center line:79%
A 100 percent home-centered
Church experience.

07:16.032 --> 07:19.069 align:center line:79%
In 1945, my grandfather
was serving in the war

07:19.102 --> 07:22.672 align:center line:79%
far away from home. When
enemies approached their farm,

07:22.872 --> 07:24.474 align:center line:81%
Oma took her two little children

07:24.474 --> 07:28.144 align:center line:79%
and left their beloved farm behind
to seek refuge in a safer place.

07:28.912 --> 07:31.348 align:center line:79%
After a difficult and life
threatening journey,

07:31.348 --> 07:35.285 align:center line:79%
they finally found refuge
in May of 1945 in northern Germany.

07:35.752 --> 07:39.089 align:center line:79%
They had nothing left except
the clothes on their bodies.

07:39.089 --> 07:41.925 align:center line:79%
But Oma continued
with what she was able to do:

07:42.125 --> 07:44.394 align:center line:81%
she prayed with her children—every day—

07:44.627 --> 07:48.164 align:center line:79%
she sang with them the songs
of Zion she had memorized by heart—

07:48.164 --> 07:51.434 align:center line:81%
every day. Life was extremely hard,

07:51.434 --> 07:55.638 align:center line:79%
and for many years focused on simply
making sure there was food on the table.

07:55.972 --> 07:59.442 align:center line:81%
But in 1955, my dad, then 17 years old,

07:59.442 --> 08:03.613 align:center line:79%
was going to trade school in the city
of Rendsburg. He walked by a building

08:03.613 --> 08:06.449 align:center line:79%
and saw a small sign
on the outside that read

08:06.449 --> 08:08.785 align:center line:79%
“Kirche Jesu Christi der Heiligen
der Letzten Tage”—

08:09.085 --> 08:11.688 align:center line:79%
“Church of Jesus Christ
of Latter-day Saints.”

08:12.055 --> 08:13.890 align:center line:81%
He thought, “That’s interesting;

08:14.124 --> 08:15.492 align:center line:81%
this is Mother’s church.”

08:15.859 --> 08:19.729 align:center line:79%
So when he came home,
he told Oma that he had found her church.

08:19.729 --> 08:24.300 align:center line:79%
You can imagine how she must have felt
after almost 25 years of no contact

08:24.300 --> 08:27.937 align:center line:79%
with the Church. She was determined
to attend the next Sunday

08:27.937 --> 08:30.106 align:center line:81%
and convinced my father to accompany her.

08:30.707 --> 08:34.844 align:center line:79%
Rensburg was more than 20 miles away
from the little village where they lived.

08:34.844 --> 08:37.981 align:center line:79%
But this would not keep
Oma from attending church.

08:37.981 --> 08:41.251 align:center line:79%
The next Sunday, she got on her bicycle
together with my father

08:41.251 --> 08:45.088 align:center line:79%
and rode to church.
When the sacrament meeting started,

08:45.088 --> 08:49.225 align:center line:79%
my dad sat down in the last
row, hoping it would be over soon.

08:50.060 --> 08:52.195 align:center line:81%
This was Oma’s Church and not his.

08:52.695 --> 08:54.998 align:center line:81%
What he saw was not very encouraging:

08:55.298 --> 08:57.333 align:center line:81%
only a few older women in attendance,

08:57.333 --> 09:01.671 align:center line:79%
and two young missionaries who effectively
ran everything in the meeting.

09:02.305 --> 09:03.873 align:center line:81%
But then they started to sing,

09:04.741 --> 09:05.909 align:center line:81%
and they sang the songs

09:05.909 --> 09:09.412 align:center line:79%
of Zion that my dad had heard
since he was a little boy:

09:10.346 --> 09:11.714 align:center line:81%
“Come, Come, Ye Saints,”

09:12.182 --> 09:15.085 align:center line:81%
“O My Father,” “Praise to the Man.”

09:15.785 --> 09:17.754 align:center line:81%
Hearing this little flock sing

09:17.754 --> 09:20.457 align:center line:79%
the songs of Zion he’d
known since childhood

09:20.457 --> 09:23.193 align:center line:81%
pierced his heart, and he knew immediately

09:23.193 --> 09:25.829 align:center line:79%
and without a doubt
that the Church was true.

09:26.463 --> 09:30.433 align:center line:79%
The first sacrament meeting my grandmother
attended after 25 years,

09:30.600 --> 09:34.070 align:center line:79%
was the meeting where my father
received a personal confirmation

09:34.070 --> 09:37.640 align:center line:79%
of the truthfulness of the restored
gospel of Jesus Christ.

09:37.640 --> 09:42.512 align:center line:79%
He was baptized three weeks later
on September 25th, 1955,

09:42.912 --> 09:45.215 align:center line:81%
together with my grandfather and my aunt.

09:47.083 --> 09:51.421 align:center line:79%
It has been more than 70 years since
that tiny sacrament meeting in Rendsburg.

09:51.421 --> 09:55.725 align:center line:79%
I often think about Oma, how she must
have felt in those lonely nights,

09:55.959 --> 09:58.962 align:center line:79%
doing the small and simple
things she was able to do,

09:59.262 --> 10:01.331 align:center line:81%
like praying, reading, and singing.

10:01.965 --> 10:05.568 align:center line:79%
As I stand here today in general
conference and talk about my Oma,

10:05.969 --> 10:09.372 align:center line:79%
her determination to keep her covenants
and trust in the Lord

10:09.372 --> 10:14.144 align:center line:79%
notwithstanding her struggles fills
my heart with humility and gratitude—

10:14.344 --> 10:18.581 align:center line:79%
not only for her, but for so many of our
wonderful Saints throughout the world

10:18.581 --> 10:22.519 align:center line:79%
who focus on the simplicity in Christ
in their challenging circumstances,

10:22.519 --> 10:24.287 align:center line:81%
perhaps seeing little change now

10:24.454 --> 10:28.558 align:center line:79%
but trusting that great things will come
to pass someday in the future.

10:29.325 --> 10:32.462 align:center line:79%
I have learned through my own
experience that this small

10:32.462 --> 10:36.199 align:center line:79%
and simple things of the gospel
and faithfully focusing on Christ

10:36.366 --> 10:39.702 align:center line:79%
lead us to true joy,
bring about mighty miracles,

10:39.702 --> 10:43.773 align:center line:79%
and grant us confidence that all promised
blessings will come to pass.

10:43.773 --> 10:47.210 align:center line:79%
This is as true
for you as it is true for me.

10:47.810 --> 10:49.879 align:center line:81%
And the words of Elder Jeffrey R. Holland,

10:49.879 --> 10:54.584 align:center line:79%
“Some blessings come soon, some come
late, and some don’t come until heaven;

10:55.185 --> 10:58.988 align:center line:79%
but for those who embrace the gospel
of Jesus Christ, they come.”

10:58.988 --> 11:03.193 align:center line:79%
Of this I also testify
in the name of Jesus Christ, amen.

